data.content:
The lightest option is .NET's built-in **`TimeProvider`** (available since .NET 8). No extra packages needed — just accept it as a constructor parameter:

```csharp
public class InvoiceCalculator(TimeProvider clock)
{
    public bool IsOverdue(DateTimeOffset dueDate)
        => clock.GetUtcNow() > dueDate;
}
```

**Production:** `new InvoiceCalculator(TimeProvider.System)` — zero behaviour change.

**Tests:** `new InvoiceCalculator(new FakeTimeProvider(fixedTime))` — fully deterministic. (`FakeTimeProvider` ships in `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing`.)

Would you like me to apply this change to `InvoiceCalculator.cs`?
